                "text": "Find the included angle using the cosine rule, then apply the triangle area rule.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $C$ be the angle between the $8\\text{ cm}$ and $13\\text{ cm}$ sides.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos C&=\\frac{8^2+13^2-15^2}{2(8)(13)}\\\\\\cos C&=\\frac{1}{26}\\\\C&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{26}\\right)\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac12(8)(13)\\sin C\\\\A&=52\\sin\\left(\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{26}\\right)\\right)\\\\A&\\approx52.0\\text{ cm}^2\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
